# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

# PostgreSQL connection string. The app throws an error at startup without this.
# Example (local):      postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/harshdev
# Example (Neon/Vercel): postgresql://user:pass@host.neon.tech/dbname?sslmode=require
DATABASE_URL=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL — Admin login fallback
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only used until you set a password via the Admin Panel's "Change Password"
# screen (which stores credentials in the database instead). If left unset,
# these default to admin / admin123 — change them before deploying publicly.
ADMIN_USERNAME=admin
ADMIN_PASSWORD=admin123

# Secret used to sign admin session tokens (see src/lib/auth.ts). If unset,
# it falls back to a value derived from ADMIN_PASSWORD, which works but is
# weaker. Recommended: set this to a long random string in production, e.g.
# generate one with: openssl rand -hex 32
ADMIN_SESSION_SECRET=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL — Persistent file storage (Cloudinary)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Without these, uploaded avatars/backgrounds/resume PDFs are written to
# local disk (./storage) — fine on a normal VM/server, but WIPED on every
# deploy/restart on ephemeral or serverless hosts (e.g. Vercel). Set all
# three to upload to Cloudinary instead, which persists. Free tier at
# https://cloudinary.com — values are on your Cloudinary Dashboard home page.
CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=
CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=
CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL — Real Razorpay donation payments
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Without these, the "Razorpay / Cards" option in the donation modal returns
# a clear 503 error telling the user to use UPI instead — it will NOT fall
# back to fabricating a fake payment. Get these from your Razorpay Dashboard
# (Settings > API Keys for the first two, Settings > Webhooks for the third
# after you create a webhook pointing at /api/donations/webhook subscribed
# to `payment.captured` and `payment.failed`).
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=
RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL — AI Chat Widget LLM synthesis
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# The AI chat works out of the box using free DuckDuckGo/Wikipedia search with
# no key required. Set ANY ONE of the keys below to enable higher-quality LLM
# answer synthesis on top of those search results. Priority order: Groq -> OpenAI
# -> Gemini -> OpenRouter (first one found is used).
GROQ_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set automatically by most hosts — no action needed
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# NODE_ENV=production
